# Mustard harness scratch — runtime state, not versioned.
.cache/
.harness/
.metrics/
.agent-state/
.agent-memory/
.pipeline-states/
.compact-state/
.session/
.dispatch/
.agent-memory/
agent-memory/
knowledge/
memory/
feature-digest.json
settings.local.json
.dashboard.pid
.dashboard.port

# Compaction memory (session-scoped, pruned after 24h by the session cleanup
# observer, which is also the only thing that ever reads it).
.compact-state/

# Work-unit worktrees (created by `work-unit-open`, pruned by git-settle).
worktrees/

# Plan-mode plan files. The peer of `scratch/` below — the write gate treats
# both as the harness's carve-out, and neither is code. It was covered only by
# the clone-local exclude, which does not travel.
plans/

# Sanctioned throwaway evidence: the write gate lets a diagnosis write here on a
# protected integration base (`work_branch_gate`), so it must be ignored by
# construction — scratch decides between hypotheses, it never joins the unit.
scratch/

# Rendered dispatch prompts (`agent-prompt-render --emit ref` writes the full
# text to a file and prints only the reference). Regenerable from the same
# render — one directory per spec, plus the spec-less one.
.dispatch/
spec/*/.dispatch/

# Per-spec event log + blob spill.
spec/*/.events/
spec/*/.blobs/

# Local editor state — written per project, regenerable, and none of it is code.
.obsidian/

# Runtime output the harness writes into `.claude/` while working. A spec's own
# content stays VERSIONED — it belongs to its unit — but these sidecars are
# regenerable, and untracked they are what blocks the exit ritual: the harness
# competing with itself for a clean tree.
#
# `spec/*/qa/report.md` is deliberately NOT here: the QA transcript is the
# unit's own record of which criteria passed, the peer of `review/verdict.md`,
# and the close commits it. Only the machine renders of it are regenerable.
# The two GATE MARKERS, and they are ignored for a reason no other line here
# shares. Everything above is ignored because it is regenerable; these two are
# ignored because versioning them would DEFEAT the gate they stand for.
#
# `.approved-by-user` is minted only from an act a model cannot author, and
# `approve-spec` decides on the file's PRESENCE, not its contents. `.clarified`
# is the same shape for the clarify gate. Committed, they would travel: a fresh
# clone would arrive with the approval already given.
spec/*/.approved-by-user
spec/*/.clarified

spec/*/.memory-approved
spec/*/.cut-base
spec/*/qa-report.json
spec/*/qa-report.html
spec/*/economy-baselines.json
spec/*/wave-*/diff.md
spec/*/wave-*/prompt.md
spec/*/wave-*/warnings.txt
